9. Why This Works

Binary Search works because the feasibility is monotonic:

If a path exists with minimum edge cost ≥ X, then it also exists for any value < X.

If X is not feasible, any value > X is also not feasible.


The DAG shortest-path DP correctly computes the minimum total cost among all allowed paths, so checking dist[n-1] ≤ k precisely determines feasibility.


---

10. Edge Cases

No path from 0 to n-1 → return -1.

Intermediate node is offline.

k = 0.

Edge cost can be 0.

Single direct edge from 0 to n-1.

Multiple paths with the same score.

Very large edge costs (10^9).

Empty edge list.



